WEBVTT

00:01.270 --> 00:03.980
SHIZUOKA PREFECTURE - NANKATSU CITY

00:02.580 --> 00:03.980
Hey, take a look at this.

00:03.980 --> 00:06.440
THE DRIVE SHOT IS COMPLETE!

00:03.980 --> 00:06.440
There's an article about Tsubasa.

00:06.440 --> 00:09.960
"Tsubasa Ozora has perfected his miraculous Drive Shot.

00:09.960 --> 00:12.720
There's only 2 matches left until Nankatsu's V3", it says.

00:12.720 --> 00:16.670
The semi-finals will be Nankatsu vs. Furano and Toho vs. Meiwa Higashi.

00:16.670 --> 00:19.470
The final's sure to be Nankatsu vs. Toho, right?

00:19.470 --> 00:21.500
Well, we still don't know about that.

00:21.500 --> 00:22.670
Urabe!

00:22.670 --> 00:29.880
Tsubasa's Drive Shot might be decisive, but it'll be hard to win against Furano's teamplay with Tsubasa alone.

00:30.320 --> 00:36.660
Moreover, of Toho's opponents, 8 of Meiwa Higashi's regulars are former Meiwa FC members,

00:30.880 --> 00:35.380
MEIWA HIGASHI MS

00:36.660 --> 00:39.390
Hyuga's friends who fought alongside him back then.

00:36.890 --> 00:39.390
MEIWA FC

00:39.390 --> 00:42.260
So, it'll be a showdown between Coach Kira's students?

00:42.260 --> 00:46.770
Meiwa Higashi also knows all about Hyuga and his friends' personalities and habits.

00:46.770 --> 00:48.420
That's not all.

00:48.420 --> 00:51.940
They are sure to put everything they've got into today's match.

00:51.940 --> 00:55.200
Just like we did in our match against Nankatsu...

00:55.960 --> 01:00.700
If Toho doesn't use Hyuga in this semi-finals match,

01:00.700 --> 01:05.330
there's no way knowing who'd win between Toho and Meiwa Higashi.

01:12.210 --> 01:14.920
<i>Ai! Ai! Ai!</i>

01:12.210 --> 01:14.920
<i>Love! Love! Love!</i>

01:15.840 --> 01:18.510
<i>Ai! Ai! Ai!</i>

01:15.840 --> 01:18.510
<i>Love! Love! Love!</i>

01:19.430 --> 01:22.140
<i>Ai! Ai! Ai!</i>

01:19.430 --> 01:22.140
<i>Love! Love! Love!</i>

01:29.020 --> 01:31.860
<i>moeru you ni hitori demo</i>

01:29.020 --> 01:31.860
<i>I keep running, lying to myself</i>

01:31.860 --> 01:38.110
<i>ikiteyukeru to usobuite hashiritsudzukete</i>

01:31.860 --> 01:38.110
<i>that I can live alone, though the loneliness makes me burn</i>

01:38.110 --> 01:44.000
<i>unubore no morosa wo kimi wa shitteta no ni</i>

01:38.110 --> 01:44.000
<i>You knew how fragile my self-conceit makes me</i>

01:44.000 --> 01:50.590
<i>kokoro made uchinomaresareta kono yoru ni</i>

01:44.000 --> 01:50.590
<i>In this night that even shattered my heart</i>

01:50.590 --> 01:54.590
<i>kimi no koe sagasu</i>

01:50.590 --> 01:54.590
<i>I hate how weak I am</i>

01:54.590 --> 01:59.090
<i>kono yowasa ga nikui yo</i>

01:54.590 --> 01:59.090
<i>yearning for your voice</i>

01:59.090 --> 02:04.680
<i>ima sugu torimodoshi ni ikanakya</i>

01:59.090 --> 02:04.680
<i>"I've got to get you back right now!"</i>

02:04.680 --> 02:06.230
<i>baka darou?</i>

02:04.680 --> 02:06.230
<i>I'm stupid, right?</i>

02:06.230 --> 02:07.440
<i>ai</i>

02:06.230 --> 02:07.440
<i>Love!</i>

02:07.440 --> 02:10.940
<i>kizudarake no ai wo shinjite</i>

02:07.440 --> 02:10.940
<i>Believing in my scarred love</i>

02:10.940 --> 02:20.820
<i>nagareochita namida sae mo tsuyosa e to kaete</i>

02:10.940 --> 02:20.820
<i>I will turn these shedded tears into strength</i>

02:20.820 --> 02:21.660
<i>ai</i>

02:20.820 --> 02:21.660
<i>Love!</i>

02:21.660 --> 02:25.450
<i>kizudarake no ai da to shite mo</i>

02:21.660 --> 02:25.450
<i>Even though it is a scarred love</i>

02:25.450 --> 02:29.460
<i>bokura no sekai wo tomoshiteru</i>

02:25.450 --> 02:29.460
<i>it lightens up our world</i>

02:29.460 --> 02:35.710
<i>kono ai mo ichido taritomo</i>

02:29.460 --> 02:35.710
<i>I will not let go of this love</i>

02:35.710 --> 02:38.510
<i>hanasanai</i>

02:35.710 --> 02:38.510
<i>for a single moment!</i>

02:40.340 --> 02:45.350
<b><b>EPISODE 43:
FIERCE TIGER LIGHTS THE FIRE</b></b>

02:42.870 --> 02:48.130
<i>In this National Middle School Football Tournament, 47 teams representing each prefecture of Japan have fought,</i>

02:48.130 --> 02:49.600
<i>and all but four teams remain!</i>

02:49.600 --> 02:52.310
<i>The first semi-finals match is about to begin!</i>

02:52.310 --> 02:55.150
<i>The host prefecture Saitama's representatives, Meiwa Higashi,</i>

02:55.150 --> 02:58.690
<i>and Tokyo representatives Toho Academy, will clash against each other.</i>

02:58.690 --> 03:02.150
<i>Both players' teams have come out onto the field.</i>

03:04.990 --> 03:07.330
<i>Toho, considered a contender to the championship,</i>

03:07.330 --> 03:12.040
<i>have been winning their matches with ease, all while saving their ace, Hyuga, for later.</i>

03:12.040 --> 03:17.710
<i>On the other side, Meiwa Higashi have won their way through, playing their characteristically offensive football.</i>

03:17.710 --> 03:19.150
<i>Just you watch, Toho.</i>

03:19.150 --> 03:21.260
<i>We'll be the ones to defeat you.</i>

03:21.940 --> 03:24.140
<i>Sawaki, we won't lose to you!</i>

03:24.140 --> 03:27.560
<i>It looks like Hyuga is on the bench today as well.</i>

03:27.560 --> 03:28.310
Hyuga!

03:28.310 --> 03:30.060
So, you're on the bench again.

03:30.060 --> 03:31.270
Hyuga...

03:35.020 --> 03:37.320
<i>This match is ours.</i>

03:38.860 --> 03:40.480
Go, Meiwa Higashi!

03:40.480 --> 03:43.870
<i>Since they're playing at home, the stands are full of Meiwa Higashi supporters.</i>

03:43.870 --> 03:47.120
<i>They will be dependable allies in this important match.</i>

03:47.120 --> 03:49.410
As expected, Hyuga is on the bench.

03:49.410 --> 03:52.870
We'll only have to watch out for Takeshi and Wakashimazu.

03:52.870 --> 03:55.680
We know everything about them:

03:55.680 --> 03:58.550
Their personalities, their play, their moves and weak points.

03:58.550 --> 04:00.880
Because we were teammates back then.

04:00.880 --> 04:04.620
We can keep Takeshi in check,
and steal a goal from Wakashimazu.

04:04.620 --> 04:08.760
If Toho doesn't have Kojiro Hyuga, we can definitely win!

04:08.760 --> 04:11.850
We'll surely defeat Toho!

04:11.850 --> 04:13.350
Yeah!

04:14.240 --> 04:19.690
<i>The first semi-finals match finally begins with Meiwa Higashi's kick-off.</i>

04:21.490 --> 04:23.490
All right, here we go!

04:23.490 --> 04:24.740
Captain!

04:31.290 --> 04:35.580
<i>As the match begins, Meiwa Higashi connect a series of passes and steadily move to attack!</i>

04:35.580 --> 04:39.210
Go go, Meiwa Higashi!

04:39.210 --> 04:41.170
As if we'd lose to the likes of you!

04:41.170 --> 04:41.840
Sawaki!

04:43.850 --> 04:46.720
<i>Meiwa Higashi's attack is flowing well!</i>

04:46.720 --> 04:48.550
The first goal will be ours!

04:50.290 --> 04:54.640
<i>In a moment, Toho's Takeshi Sawada stops Meiwa Higashi's fierce attack flat!</i>

04:55.690 --> 04:56.940
Well played.

04:56.940 --> 04:57.930
<i>We will win!</i>

04:57.930 --> 05:01.190
<i>This is the last match we'll have to play without Hyuga.</i>

05:01.710 --> 05:03.030
<i>Takeshi...</i>

05:03.030 --> 05:07.660
<i>Meiwa Higashi send two players
to stop Toho's playmaker, Sawada.</i>

05:07.660 --> 05:09.490
<i>Come on, Takeshi!</i>

05:09.490 --> 05:13.160
<i>You are younger than us,
there's no way we'd lose to you!</i>

05:13.830 --> 05:14.540
Here!

05:14.540 --> 05:17.040
<i>Sawada completes his work with a pass.</i>

05:18.280 --> 05:20.290
<i>But his pass has been read!</i>

05:20.790 --> 05:22.590
<i>It isn't able to reach Sorimachi!</i>

05:22.590 --> 05:25.170
We can read you like an open book.

05:25.840 --> 05:26.800
Take this!

05:26.800 --> 05:29.300
<i>Meiwa Higashi is on the attack again!</i>

05:30.180 --> 05:32.810
Meiwa Higashi are moving well today.

05:32.810 --> 05:36.190
Toho in particular is a special opponent for Meiwa Higashi.

05:36.190 --> 05:40.190
They must have focused their eyes solely on this match and really prepared for it.

05:40.190 --> 05:41.360
Sawaki!

05:42.530 --> 05:45.900
<i>Meiwa Higashi quickly get into firing range.</i>

05:45.900 --> 05:47.990
Eat this!

05:47.990 --> 05:51.370
<i>Meiwa Higashi's Sawaki fires the first shot of the match!</i>

05:51.370 --> 05:52.240
It's on target!

05:53.270 --> 05:54.340
<i>He got it!</i>

05:54.340 --> 05:56.540
<i>Goalkeeper Wakashimazu with a diving catch!</i>

05:56.540 --> 05:58.040
Nice, Wakashimazu!

05:58.040 --> 06:00.920
<i>He's not called the #1 goalkeeper
of the tournament for nothing!</i>

06:00.920 --> 06:03.630
<i>Wakashimazu keeps his clean sheet yet again!</i>

06:05.750 --> 06:07.430
<i>Well, that's Wakashimazu for you.</i>

06:07.430 --> 06:09.350
<i>But we're just getting started...</i>

06:09.350 --> 06:11.550
<i>I'll definitely score one against you!</i>

06:13.310 --> 06:14.430
Run!

06:15.560 --> 06:17.890
<i>The ball reaches Sorimachi, the forward.</i>

06:17.890 --> 06:19.060
Sorimachi!

06:19.730 --> 06:22.190
<i>This is another favorite tactic of Toho's!</i>

06:23.390 --> 06:25.310
<i>And here, this pass is also cut!</i>

06:25.310 --> 06:27.530
<i>Meiwa Higashi has read this play, too!</i>

06:27.530 --> 06:28.610
Over here!

06:30.430 --> 06:33.410
<i>We're already 20 minutes into the first half,</i>

06:33.410 --> 06:35.470
<i>and neither team has scored thus far.</i>

06:35.470 --> 06:38.080
<i>The tense balance of this 0-0 remains undisturbed.</i>

06:38.640 --> 06:43.590
<i>The combination play between the center forward
Sorimachi, who's been filling in for Toho's ace Hyuga,</i>

06:43.590 --> 06:47.090
<i>and Sawada, Toho's young playmaker, is completely sealed off!</i>

06:47.090 --> 06:49.150
<i>They can't find a chance to score.</i>

06:49.150 --> 06:50.010
<i>All right!</i>

06:50.010 --> 06:52.410
This isn't good. My passes aren't working.

06:52.970 --> 06:55.680
<i>Though it feels as if Meiwa Higashi is slightly in control,</i>

06:57.420 --> 07:02.900
<i>Wakashimazu's several fine saves continue to block them from the goal, and so they remain scoreless.</i>

07:02.210 --> 07:02.900
Damn it!

07:03.410 --> 07:05.190
For you, Takeshi!

07:07.410 --> 07:09.090
<i>Sawada brings the ball upfield!</i>

07:09.090 --> 07:11.450
<i>Who will he send a pass to next?</i>

07:12.000 --> 07:14.580
<i>Sorimachi is being marked.</i>

07:14.580 --> 07:15.280
Here!

07:15.280 --> 07:16.350
<i>He sends it to the side.</i>

07:16.350 --> 07:16.830
Got it!

07:17.330 --> 07:17.650
Ah!

07:17.650 --> 07:20.160
<i>Meiwa Higashi has cut it yet again!</i>

07:20.160 --> 07:21.250
It's no use.

07:21.250 --> 07:23.630
Every one of my moves is being read.

07:23.630 --> 07:26.250
If only Hyuga was here now...

07:34.500 --> 07:39.600
<i>Unfortunately, just as Meiwa Higashi was about to mount one last attack, the whistle is blown!</i>

07:39.600 --> 07:42.100
<i>The first half ends scoreless on both sides.</i>

07:43.060 --> 07:49.070
<i>It's the first time the championship contender Toho enters halftime without having scored.</i>

07:51.690 --> 07:54.280
Toho is being pushed down.

07:54.280 --> 07:54.910
Yes.

07:54.910 --> 07:57.540
This match will be hard for them without Hyuga.

08:03.540 --> 08:06.670
MEIWA HIGASHI MIDDLE SCHOOL
SAITAMA PREFECTURE

08:03.540 --> 08:06.670
All right! Our defense was flawless in the first half.

08:06.670 --> 08:08.400
All we need to do is to score.

08:08.400 --> 08:10.170
We have to score one at all costs!

08:10.170 --> 08:14.300
If we keep attacking like this, surely, a decisive chance will come!

08:14.870 --> 08:16.360
Don't let that chance pass by!

08:16.360 --> 08:17.300
Yes, sir!

08:17.300 --> 08:18.890
TOHO ACADEMY
TOKYO

08:18.890 --> 08:19.970
Damn it!

08:19.970 --> 08:22.060
We're totally being swept away by their pace.

08:22.060 --> 08:24.190
How can they steal the ball from us so easily...?

08:24.190 --> 08:26.450
If this keeps up, things won't end well.

08:29.390 --> 08:31.170
Okay guys, gather around.

08:35.070 --> 08:38.930
Sawada. You're being completely read.

08:38.930 --> 08:40.330
I don't mind if you take risks.

08:40.330 --> 08:44.050
Change your tactics a little bit in the second half; try changing your position.

08:44.050 --> 08:45.560
Y-yes.

08:45.560 --> 08:47.710
Sorimachi, keep actively aiming to score.

08:47.710 --> 08:49.340
Take long shots if necessary.

08:49.340 --> 08:52.420
Their goalkeeper is nowhere as good as Wakashimazu.

08:52.420 --> 08:54.180
Just fire away any chance you get.

08:54.180 --> 08:54.970
Yes!

08:54.970 --> 08:56.100
Are we clear?

08:56.100 --> 08:57.970
We'll definitely win this match!

08:57.970 --> 08:59.910
There'll be no member changes.

08:59.910 --> 09:02.180
We'll keep the same members from the first half.

09:02.180 --> 09:03.850
Yes...

09:04.470 --> 09:08.910
<i>If only Captain was playing, this game would have been so much easier...</i>

09:11.110 --> 09:13.040
What are you going to do on his case, Mr. Mikami?

09:13.040 --> 09:18.030
He surely has the skills, but Kojiro Hyuga hasn't played at all this tournament.

09:18.030 --> 09:19.120
Indeed.

09:19.120 --> 09:21.350
<i>3-0...</i>

09:21.350 --> 09:24.620
<i>If I was playing, the score would be 3-0 in this match.</i>

09:24.620 --> 09:26.070
<i>Damn it.</i>

09:26.070 --> 09:30.170
<i>If they get ahead of us in the second half, I'll go...</i>

09:30.170 --> 09:32.550
<i>I'll force my way onto the pitch and play!</i>

09:34.920 --> 09:38.760
<i>The second half will start with Toho Academy's kick-off.</i>

09:36.800 --> 09:39.470
Good luck, Toho!

09:40.510 --> 09:43.110
<i>Whatever happens, only 30 minutes remain.</i>

09:43.110 --> 09:45.270
<i>Which team will advance to the grand finals?</i>

09:45.270 --> 09:49.020
Go go, Meiwa Higashi!

09:49.790 --> 09:53.150
<i>Maybe it's only natural that they can read through my moves...</i>

09:53.150 --> 09:56.780
<i>Most of Meiwa Higashi's players are my friends from Meiwa FC.</i>

09:56.780 --> 09:59.740
<i>I played with them when I was in elementary school.</i>

09:59.740 --> 10:03.560
<i>Moreover, they were all trained by Coach Kira.</i>

10:03.560 --> 10:05.410
<i>They are not your average players.</i>

10:05.410 --> 10:11.500
<i>If it were Tsubasa, another midfielder like me... I wonder, how would he break through?</i>

10:11.500 --> 10:13.500
<i>If only Hyuga was...</i>

10:14.490 --> 10:15.460
I've got this!

10:15.460 --> 10:17.720
<i>Sawada easily gives up the ball!</i>

10:17.720 --> 10:18.800
Oh no!

10:18.800 --> 10:20.300
Nice cut!

10:20.300 --> 10:22.670
<i>Meiwa Higashi swiftly proceeds to attack!</i>

10:22.670 --> 10:24.810
<i>Will Meiwa Higashi set the pace this half as well?</i>

10:24.810 --> 10:27.710
Being read so easily has caused him to lose his composure.

10:27.710 --> 10:28.410
Eh?

10:28.410 --> 10:32.060
Maybe being a playmaker is too much of a burden for a first-grader like Sawada.

10:32.060 --> 10:33.530
<i>What am I doing?</i>

10:33.530 --> 10:36.320
<i>If I keep acting like this, we'll get caught in their pace again.</i>

10:36.320 --> 10:37.570
<i>Takeshi...</i>

10:37.570 --> 10:38.320
I'll stop you!

10:38.690 --> 10:39.570
Ah!

10:39.990 --> 10:41.490
<i>It's a corner kick.</i>

10:41.490 --> 10:43.450
<i>It's the first corner of the second half.</i>

10:43.450 --> 10:45.120
All right, now's our chance!

10:45.120 --> 10:46.760
This is our fourth corner kick.

10:46.760 --> 10:48.960
This might just be our chance.

10:48.960 --> 10:50.960
Imai! Go further right!

10:50.960 --> 10:53.330
<i>Toho is closing their ranks in front of the goal.</i>

10:53.330 --> 10:55.250
<i>Wakashimazu gives out his orders.</i>

10:55.250 --> 10:57.210
<i>Kawagoe will take the corner kick.</i>

10:57.210 --> 11:00.780
<i>If I screw this one up, Wakashimazu will just catch it.</i>

11:00.780 --> 11:04.220
<i>First, I should send the ball somewhere he can't reach...</i>

11:05.270 --> 11:05.970
Here!

11:05.970 --> 11:07.970
<i>It's far away from the goal!</i>

11:07.970 --> 11:09.970
<i>Wakashimazu can't jump out to get it!</i>

11:10.540 --> 11:11.850
Got it!

11:11.850 --> 11:13.270
Let's do this, guys!

11:14.480 --> 11:15.710
Go!

11:15.710 --> 11:17.860
<i>Meiwa Higashi attack with all their members!</i>

11:17.860 --> 11:18.620
What?

11:18.620 --> 11:19.820
Clear it!

11:19.820 --> 11:22.200
<i>Toho go to stop them at full force!</i>

11:22.200 --> 11:25.490
<i>It's a big chance for Hori, who is right in front of the goal!</i>

11:25.490 --> 11:27.240
Go!

11:27.240 --> 11:28.170
What?!

11:28.170 --> 11:29.450
<i>He stopped it!</i>

11:29.450 --> 11:32.750
<i>He's managed to react to this shot, which looked like a done deal!</i>

11:32.750 --> 11:35.250
<i>But the ball is still in play!</i>

11:35.900 --> 11:38.260
Please, clear it! Just clear the ball!

11:38.260 --> 11:39.510
Let's go!

11:39.510 --> 11:41.260
We'll defend! Clear the ball!

11:41.260 --> 11:42.550
<i>Who will be faster?!</i>

11:42.550 --> 11:43.760
<i>The shot or the clearance?!</i>

11:44.090 --> 11:45.000
Eat this!

11:45.000 --> 11:47.930
This is the offensive football Coach Kira left us!

11:47.930 --> 11:48.850
What?!

11:48.850 --> 11:52.060
Meiwa's Special Sliding Squad takes off!

11:53.810 --> 11:55.860
We've got you!

11:55.860 --> 11:57.520
There's no way I'll let you...!

12:04.660 --> 12:06.530
<i>It's in!</i>

12:06.530 --> 12:09.160
<i>Meiwa Higashi's persistence bears fruit!</i>

12:09.160 --> 12:11.910
<i>The first goal of the match is by Meiwa Higashi!</i>

12:22.970 --> 12:26.470
<i>Finally, the tense 0-0 deadlock has been broken!</i>

12:27.520 --> 12:31.770
<i>Meiwa Higashi finished the loose ball Wakashimazu deflected with a sliding shot.</i>

12:31.770 --> 12:37.560
<i>Toho's defense, along with their proud iron wall, have finally conceded their first goal in this tournament!</i>

12:37.560 --> 12:39.860
Toho let them get ahead.

12:42.360 --> 12:43.610
We did it! {boiz!}

12:43.610 --> 12:45.200
We scored a goal!

12:45.200 --> 12:48.200
<i>They celebrate as the scoreboard finally changes.</i>

12:48.200 --> 12:52.330
<i>With this, Meiwa Higashi move one step closer to the grand finals!</i>

12:55.660 --> 12:56.710
Captain!

12:56.710 --> 12:58.040
Stop there, Hyuga!

12:58.790 --> 13:00.210
That's Hyuga.

13:00.210 --> 13:00.840
Hyuga!

13:00.840 --> 13:02.010
Kojiro!

13:02.010 --> 13:03.550
Captain...

13:03.550 --> 13:04.880
Coach.

13:04.880 --> 13:06.970
What exactly are you doing?

13:06.970 --> 13:09.390
I don't intend on letting you play this match.

13:09.390 --> 13:11.100
Sit down, Hyuga.

13:11.100 --> 13:12.680
Those are my orders!

13:15.570 --> 13:19.060
Orders... Orders, orders...!

13:20.090 --> 13:22.610
Who died and made you king of the world?!

13:22.610 --> 13:25.200
Where do you get off thinking you're always right?!

13:25.590 --> 13:26.360
What?

13:27.350 --> 13:32.790
Why? Why can't I just play a match?!

13:33.180 --> 13:34.580
Captain...

13:42.460 --> 13:43.880
Stop, Hyuga!

13:43.880 --> 13:45.500
Guys, don't lose now!

13:45.500 --> 13:46.800
It's just a one score lead!

13:46.800 --> 13:48.800
You have plenty of time!

13:48.800 --> 13:51.730
You guys are more than able to turn this one around!

13:51.730 --> 13:54.560
But, just this once, you've gotta do it without me!

13:54.560 --> 13:56.940
I'm begging you, guys!

13:56.940 --> 13:58.060
Hyuga.

13:58.060 --> 13:59.220
Captain...

13:59.220 --> 14:00.690
Hyuga.

14:01.210 --> 14:04.440
No matter what, I will play in the finals!

14:06.700 --> 14:08.000
Hyuga.

14:10.740 --> 14:12.580
All right. Let's do this, everyone!

14:12.580 --> 14:13.990
It's just as our captain said.

14:13.990 --> 14:15.210
It's just a one score lead.

14:15.210 --> 14:16.830
Let's get our payback, quickly!

14:19.160 --> 14:19.960
Yeah!

14:19.960 --> 14:22.040
We've won without our captain before.

14:22.040 --> 14:24.840
Let's show them everything Toho is capable of!

14:24.840 --> 14:27.090
We'll definitely win this match!

14:27.090 --> 14:28.330
<i>That's right!</i>

14:28.330 --> 14:35.210
<i>Before this match, we all swore we would win without Hyuga.</i>

14:35.210 --> 14:40.060
<i>We also swore that, if the coach didn't allow Hyuga to play in tomorrow's grand finals,</i>

14:40.060 --> 14:43.020
<i>we would boycott the match outright.</i>

14:43.490 --> 14:45.530
<i>Just you watch, Captain!</i>

14:45.970 --> 14:47.530
Guys...

14:47.530 --> 14:49.530
<i>The match resumes!</i>

14:49.530 --> 14:53.480
<i>What kind of offense will Toho put together while trailing by a goal?</i>

14:53.480 --> 14:54.300
You got it, guys?

14:54.300 --> 14:55.540
We'll catch up, no matter what!

14:55.540 --> 14:56.580
Yeah!!

14:56.580 --> 15:00.670
<i>Hah, we know every single move your playmaker Takeshi might try.</i>

15:00.670 --> 15:04.000
<i>That goal was enough to punch our ticket to the finals!</i>

15:05.840 --> 15:06.960
Let's go!

15:06.960 --> 15:11.340
<i>Toho fiercely advances into Meiwa's side,
desperate for an equalizer.</i>

15:11.340 --> 15:13.340
Don't let them ever move freely!

15:13.340 --> 15:18.270
<i>However, Meiwa Higashi's defense is superb today, rightfully earning full marks!</i>

15:18.270 --> 15:23.800
<i>Will this defense prove too difficult for Toho to break with Hyuga, their ace, absent from the field?</i>

15:23.800 --> 15:25.110
Guys...

15:25.110 --> 15:28.940
<i>If we can play up to Toho's standard
in this game, we can surely win.</i>

15:28.940 --> 15:30.030
Take this!

15:30.990 --> 15:32.630
<i>He is certainly being read!</i>

15:32.630 --> 15:34.250
<i>Sawada's passes won't connect!</i>

15:34.250 --> 15:34.990
Damn!

15:34.990 --> 15:36.000
What?!

15:36.000 --> 15:38.000
<i>He steals it back in a blink!</i>

15:38.000 --> 15:39.250
Nice one, Takeshi!

15:39.250 --> 15:41.540
That's it! That's the spirit, Takeshi!

15:42.230 --> 15:43.900
<i>If they steal it from you, take it back.</i>

15:43.900 --> 15:45.790
<i>That's all you've got to do.</i>

15:45.790 --> 15:47.550
<i>Isn't that right, Tsubasa...?</i>

15:47.550 --> 15:51.680
<i>I'll be a scoring midfielder like you, too.</i>

15:51.680 --> 15:52.880
Stop him!

15:52.880 --> 15:54.180
Crap!

15:54.180 --> 15:56.720
<i>Sawada skillfully dribbles his way through the midfield.</i>

15:56.720 --> 15:58.270
He's going to shoot!

15:58.270 --> 15:59.720
Block him off!

15:59.720 --> 16:02.450
<i>My former upperclassmen... I've improved myself, too!</i>

16:02.450 --> 16:04.720
<i>Sawada gets ready to shoot!</i>

16:04.720 --> 16:06.150
I won't let you score a goal!

16:06.770 --> 16:08.270
Take this!

16:08.270 --> 16:09.280
What?!

16:09.280 --> 16:09.940
Takeshi!

16:09.940 --> 16:11.940
That's your move, Tsubasa.

16:13.410 --> 16:16.570
<i>The pass connects Sorimachi for the first time!</i>

16:16.570 --> 16:24.670
Until our Captain returns, the center forward's job is mine!

16:26.080 --> 16:27.880
<i>It's in!</i>

16:27.880 --> 16:29.500
Yes! Nice shot!

16:29.500 --> 16:36.180
<i>Toho scored the equalizer in the 15th minute of the second half with a brilliant combination play! It's now 1-1!</i>

16:36.180 --> 16:37.330
We did it!

16:37.330 --> 16:38.530
We did it, Captain!

16:38.530 --> 16:39.620
Hyuga!

16:39.620 --> 16:40.520
Guys!

16:41.200 --> 16:43.400
We finally tied the game!

16:43.400 --> 16:45.040
<i>Nice shooting, Sorimachi!</i>

16:45.040 --> 16:48.520
<i>And Takeshi, it was a great decision to change from a shot to a pass!</i>

16:48.520 --> 16:50.970
<i>Now, we can't lose.</i>

16:50.970 --> 16:56.780
<i>Because I won't let our opponent score again, no matter what!</i>

17:01.290 --> 17:03.960
Toho was panicking since they didn't score in the first half,

17:03.960 --> 17:05.880
but now they've got their confidence back.

17:06.540 --> 17:09.790
That one goal was all thanks to Hyuga lighting their fire.

17:10.220 --> 17:11.200
Damn.

17:11.200 --> 17:12.960
It's still a tie.

17:12.960 --> 17:16.840
<i>Toho are riding their momentum after tying and continuing their attack.</i>

17:16.840 --> 17:18.180
Go!

17:18.180 --> 17:19.600
Let's pull ahead at once, guys!

17:20.150 --> 17:22.720
<i>The game's fallen completely into Toho's pace, now.</i>

17:22.720 --> 17:27.980
<i>Toho's doggedly fought together as a unit to make up for Hyuga's absence this tournament.</i>

17:27.980 --> 17:34.530
<i>Because of that, their teamwork improved and individual skills were honed to a keen edge.</i>

17:34.530 --> 17:37.990
<i>If you were to add Hyuga to this team now, they'd be terrifying.</i>

17:37.990 --> 17:41.550
<i>There are but scant minutes left in this match!</i>

17:41.550 --> 17:47.280
<i>If it ends like this, considering Toho has the #1 goalkeeper in the tournament in Wakashimazu,</i>

17:47.280 --> 17:49.630
<i>Meiwa Higashi will be at a huge disadvantage!</i>

17:49.630 --> 17:53.130
A tie game is basically a loss for Meiwa Higashi.

17:53.130 --> 17:55.630
We can't lose after coming this far!

17:55.630 --> 17:58.550
Guys! Don't you dare settle for a tie game!

17:58.550 --> 18:02.010
Toho's football is about winning at all costs!

18:02.010 --> 18:02.810
Yeah!

18:02.810 --> 18:05.930
<i>Should I just admit that he's Toho's captain after all?</i>

18:05.930 --> 18:10.750
<i>Hyuga... the boy who abandoned his friends, and went missing at such a critical time,</i>

18:10.750 --> 18:14.110
<i>right after our victory in the preliminaries, on our way to Nationals.</i>

18:14.110 --> 18:17.030
Yeah! Don't be afraid, Sorimachi!

18:14.110 --> 18:18.820
<i>Despite it all, our players still trust this boy... Kojiro Hyuga.</i>

18:17.030 --> 18:18.820
You can do it yourself, too!

18:21.110 --> 18:23.290
It's no good if all we do is defend.

18:23.290 --> 18:24.870
We have to attack somehow...

18:24.870 --> 18:25.870
No.

18:25.870 --> 18:27.370
Let them keep this up.

18:28.430 --> 18:31.380
We'll wait for a single counter attack, and grasp our chance!

18:31.380 --> 18:34.000
It's all we've got if we want to score against Wakashimazu.

18:34.530 --> 18:36.460
All right, got it.

18:40.010 --> 18:40.680
Sorimachi!

18:41.410 --> 18:43.300
<i>Toho's Sorimachi is sent the b—</i>

18:43.770 --> 18:44.750
<i>They couldn't!</i>

18:44.750 --> 18:46.810
<i>Meiwa Higashi intercepts this pass!</i>

18:46.810 --> 18:48.100
Okay, now!

18:48.100 --> 18:50.560
<i>It's a quick long pass!</i>

18:50.560 --> 18:53.310
<i>An instant counter attack!</i>

18:53.770 --> 18:54.820
<i>The pass makes it!</i>

18:54.820 --> 18:58.820
<i>Toho was so busy on offense that their defense is left full of holes!</i>

18:58.820 --> 19:00.070
Oh no!

19:00.070 --> 19:02.530
<i>No one is chasing after Sawaki!</i>

19:03.740 --> 19:04.870
This is bad, Toho!

19:05.840 --> 19:07.540
You thought I'd let you?!

19:07.540 --> 19:09.790
Woah, that's Wakashimazu for you.

19:09.790 --> 19:13.790
Outside the penalty area, you are just another field player, even as a goalkeeper!

19:13.790 --> 19:16.170
We will aim for win rather than a tie game!

19:16.170 --> 19:17.380
Wakashimazu.

19:17.380 --> 19:19.130
Damn you, looking down on us!

19:19.130 --> 19:20.170
Crush him!

19:20.170 --> 19:23.730
If we steal the ball from Wakashimazu, it will be a free goal!

19:23.730 --> 19:25.680
This is the chance we've waited for!

19:25.680 --> 19:31.940
And yet, the further I get past you all, the less guarded your defense is!

19:31.940 --> 19:32.900
What?!

19:32.900 --> 19:34.020
Takeshi!

19:35.410 --> 19:36.020
Take it!

19:36.020 --> 19:37.740
<i>The ball reaches Sorimachi!</i>

19:37.740 --> 19:38.780
<i>Will he shoot?</i>

19:38.780 --> 19:40.110
Don't let him shoot!

19:40.740 --> 19:42.990
<i>Oh, this pass is sent backwards!</i>

19:42.990 --> 19:43.780
What?!

19:43.780 --> 19:47.740
<i>There! Wakashimazu is running towards the ball!</i>

19:47.740 --> 19:49.870
Wakashimazu!

19:49.870 --> 19:51.120
It's all you, Wakashimazu!

19:52.560 --> 19:54.790
<i>The goalkeeper Wakashimazu shoots the ball!</i>

19:57.130 --> 19:58.490
<i>It's in!</i>

19:58.490 --> 20:01.300
<i>A terrifyingly powerful shot from Wakashimazu!</i>

20:01.300 --> 20:05.040
<i>He's brought them a comeback just before the match ends, 2-1!</i>

20:05.040 --> 20:06.800
You did it, Wakashimazu!

20:06.800 --> 20:08.880
What an awesome attack from Toho!

20:08.880 --> 20:09.560
Yeah.

20:09.560 --> 20:10.560
Damn!

20:10.560 --> 20:11.720
We'd forgotten that.

20:11.720 --> 20:14.100
Wakashimazu was originally a forward!

20:14.100 --> 20:17.130
But Meiwa FC had Hyuga, so upon Coach Kira's request,

20:17.130 --> 20:19.320
in order for us to be able to win the championship,

20:19.320 --> 20:22.110
he switched over to being a goalkeeper, instead.

20:22.630 --> 20:23.440
Tch.

20:23.440 --> 20:25.110
We knew this!

20:25.110 --> 20:31.120
With his defense and offense, Wakashimazu truly is Japan's #1 goalkeeper.

20:31.120 --> 20:35.000
<i>You took 2 goals from that Wakashimazu, Jun.</i>

20:35.000 --> 20:40.050
<i>I really want to help you be able to play football full-time like others.</i>

20:40.870 --> 20:43.960
<i>The whistle signaling the end of the match has been blown!</i>

20:43.960 --> 20:48.220
<i>Toho are the first to make their way to the finals!</i>

20:48.220 --> 20:50.380
We did it, Captain! We won!

20:50.380 --> 20:51.220
Hyuga!

20:51.220 --> 20:52.190
That's it!

20:52.190 --> 20:53.320
Great job!

20:53.320 --> 20:54.980
Great job, you guys!

20:56.730 --> 20:58.270
Wakashimazu, you were awesome!

20:58.270 --> 20:58.840
Yes, sir!

20:58.840 --> 21:00.260
You as well, Takeshi.

21:00.260 --> 21:01.230
Hyuga!

21:01.230 --> 21:03.530
And you, Sorimachi, it was a great shot!

21:03.530 --> 21:04.990
We lost.

21:04.990 --> 21:09.490
We were confident that we could defeat Toho without Hyuga in their team.

21:09.490 --> 21:12.480
No, Hyuga's strength was huge, actually.

21:13.540 --> 21:18.920
Even on the bench, Hyuga was a huge boon to Toho today.

21:18.920 --> 21:23.880
If he hadn't fired them up, we might have gotten away with this.

21:23.880 --> 21:26.880
Toho really is all about Hyuga.

21:27.310 --> 21:29.150
Katagiri, I've decided.

21:29.150 --> 21:32.470
Even if he doesn't get to play a single match this tournament,

21:32.470 --> 21:38.420
I will bring Kojiro Hyuga to Europe as Japan's center forward.

21:39.820 --> 21:40.690
Takeshi!

21:40.690 --> 21:41.400
Huh?

21:41.400 --> 21:44.970
Win the finals tomorrow and become the champions!

21:44.970 --> 21:46.740
You defeated us!

21:46.740 --> 21:49.300
Counting on you, our little underclassman from Meiwa FC!

21:49.300 --> 21:50.700
Sure!

21:50.700 --> 21:54.200
Wakashimazu! Do whatever you can to keep them at zero tomorrow.

21:54.200 --> 21:58.460
If you do that, then we will be the only ones who managed to score against you!

21:58.970 --> 22:00.840
Yeah, I'll do my best!

22:00.840 --> 22:02.670
You better win!

22:05.980 --> 22:08.550
Okay guys, it's our turn now!

22:10.050 --> 22:12.310
<i>It's on, Matsuyama.</i>

22:12.310 --> 22:15.060
<i>Just what I was hoping for, Tsubasa!</i>

22:38.710 --> 22:44.750
<i>chotto are mi na ace ga tooru</i>

22:38.710 --> 22:44.750
<i>Hey, look over there at the ace passing through</i>

22:44.750 --> 22:50.760
<i>suguremono zo to machijû sawagu</i>

22:44.750 --> 22:50.760
<i>He's the best, and the whole town cheers him on</i>

22:50.760 --> 22:56.810
<i>chô-chô samba, zigzag samba</i>

22:50.760 --> 22:56.810
<i>Butterfly samba, zig-zag samba</i>

22:56.810 --> 23:01.440
<i>aitsu no uwasa de chamba mo hashiru</i>

22:56.810 --> 23:01.440
<i>Even little old ladies go around talking about him</i>

23:03.060 --> 23:07.740
<i>sore ni tsukete mo ore-tacha nan na no</i>

23:03.060 --> 23:07.740
<i>So, even if we have him, who are we?</i>

23:09.070 --> 23:15.160
<i>ball hitotsu ni kiri-kiri mai sa</i>

23:09.070 --> 23:15.160
<i>The ball spins round and round</i>

23:15.160 --> 23:21.210
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:21.210 --> 23:25.670
<i>itsuka kimeru ze inazuma shoot</i>

23:21.210 --> 23:25.670
<i>One day, I'll score with a lightning shot!</i>

23:26.960 --> 23:33.300
<i>son toki ore ga super hero sa</i>

23:26.960 --> 23:33.300
<i>When that happens, I'll become a super hero!</i>

23:33.300 --> 23:39.350
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:39.350 --> 23:45.650
<i>moete seishun kakenukero</i>

23:39.350 --> 23:45.650
<i>This fierce youth is on the field!</i>

23:49.440 --> 23:59.030
COMING UP, EPISODE 44:
#10 VS. #10
